<?xml version="1.0"?>
<section xml:id="lists_deletion-program">
  <title>Programming Phase 1: Planning</title>
  <p>
    Let's write a function that deletes all the negative elements in a list; if you give it the list <c>[10, -66, -47, 11, 505, -217]</c>, the list will be modified to <c>[10, 11, 505]</c>. This function will <em>not</em> return a new list; it will modify the list we give it <q>in place</q>.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Here's the plan: use a <c>for</c> loop that counts from 0 to the list length minus one. If the entry at a given index is negative, we delete the element using <c>del</c>.  Sounds like a plan. Let's see it in action:
  </p>
    
  <program xml:id="del_program_plan1" interactive="activecode" language="python">
    <code>
def remove_negative(a_list):
    """Modify input list to remove all negative numbers."""
    for index in range(len(a_list)):
        if a_list[index] &lt; 0:
            del a_list[index]
        

numbers = [10, -66, -47, 11, 505, -217]
remove_negative(numbers)
print(f"Final list is {numbers}")
        </code>
  </program>
  
  <p>
    Well. That didn't work. Why did we end up with <c>IndexError: list index out of range</c>? Before you try fixing the problem, please read the next page.
  </p>
</section>
